1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:01,016
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,016 --> 00:00:02,016
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,016 --> 00:00:03,616
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,616 --> 00:00:06,749
[Episode 14]

5
00:00:16,152 --> 00:00:18,188
<i>A woman? Are you sure?</i>

6
00:00:18,188 --> 00:00:20,668
It's not like I can't tell
a man from a woman.

7
00:00:20,668 --> 00:00:23,508
That man I saw before,
he really is Kingfisher.

8
00:00:23,508 --> 00:00:25,412
I spotted Kingfisher taking aim,
and got caught.

9
00:00:25,412 --> 00:00:27,176
<i>It's extremely rare for a serial killer</i>

10
00:00:27,176 --> 00:00:30,176
like Kingfisher to suddenly
abandon his beliefs.

11
00:00:30,176 --> 00:00:32,396
Female, estimated to be in her 30s?

12
00:00:32,396 --> 00:00:34,749
<i>Wow. What is this?</i>

13
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:37,708
Yeah, what is it?

14
00:00:37,708 --> 00:00:39,424
I'm a little busy right now.

15
00:00:55,583 --> 00:00:58,396
[Caller ID Restricted:
Yoo Bo Na is waiting in Seonyudo]

16
00:00:58,396 --> 00:01:00,536
Move out? At this hour?

17
00:01:00,536 --> 00:01:02,128
Where are you going?

18
00:01:02,128 --> 00:01:03,520
What? Seonyudo Island?

19
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:05,268
Wow, even the SWAT team?

20
00:01:05,268 --> 00:01:07,136
That is on another level.

21
00:01:07,136 --> 00:01:09,164
Watch out and stay safe.

22
00:01:09,164 --> 00:01:11,596
Hey, when are you going to meet me?

23
00:01:11,596 --> 00:01:14,149
You said you'd spar with me. Remember?

24
00:01:16,684 --> 00:01:19,172
Tae Seong! Where are you going?

25
00:01:19,172 --> 00:01:20,872
Tae Seong!

26
00:01:27,049 --> 00:01:28,949
[Big Precious]

27
00:01:56,512 --> 00:01:59,424
It's not fair. What we do...

28
00:01:59,424 --> 00:02:01,616
isn't all that different.

29
00:02:01,616 --> 00:02:04,649
I'm warning you.

30
00:02:04,649 --> 00:02:09,292
If you lay a finger on
my husband or my child,

31
00:02:09,292 --> 00:02:10,992
I'll...

32
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,928
make you experience hell
while you're still alive.

33
00:02:13,928 --> 00:02:15,272
Is that so?

34
00:02:15,272 --> 00:02:17,949
Then you can experience hell
while you're alive too.

35
00:02:17,949 --> 00:02:20,796
Get destroyed just like me.

36
00:02:20,796 --> 00:02:23,483
Forget everything you hold dear.

37
00:02:33,308 --> 00:02:36,616
Think you'll still be able to
play the saint then?

38
00:03:04,524 --> 00:03:08,016
Ugh, I'm one step behind again.

39
00:03:37,792 --> 00:03:40,949
Again, our priority is
to take the suspect alive.

40
00:03:40,949 --> 00:03:41,949
Yes, sir.

41
00:03:41,949 --> 00:03:43,116
All units, listen up.

42
00:03:43,116 --> 00:03:46,616
The suspect must be taken alive. Understood?

43
00:03:47,488 --> 00:03:49,412
Teams 1 and 2, this way. Team 3, that way.

44
00:03:49,412 --> 00:03:51,112
Move in!

45
00:04:07,092 --> 00:04:08,488
Why'd you stop?

46
00:04:08,488 --> 00:04:10,283
Keep going!

47
00:04:11,724 --> 00:04:13,352
Try to kill me!

48
00:04:13,352 --> 00:04:15,832
Right in front of your husband.

49
00:04:15,832 --> 00:04:17,849
Just like you always do.

50
00:04:58,132 --> 00:05:00,912
<i>Eleven o'clock!
Suspect believed to be on the rooftop.</i>

51
00:05:00,912 --> 00:05:03,744
Over there! Team 1, follow me.
Team 2, cover us!

52
00:05:03,744 --> 00:05:05,444
Move!

53
00:05:12,216 --> 00:05:16,649
Yoo Bo Na, enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.

54
00:06:05,012 --> 00:06:07,344
Dong Jin's here. We have to go.

55
00:06:07,344 --> 00:06:09,124
Okay?

56
00:06:09,124 --> 00:06:11,956
We have to go. Hurry. Okay?

57
00:06:11,956 --> 00:06:14,136
Hurry.

58
00:06:14,136 --> 00:06:15,836
Hurry.

59
00:06:25,268 --> 00:06:28,516
<i>What? He knew everything?</i>

60
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:33,092
<i>If the blade cannot be stopped,
let it come to me.</i>

61
00:06:33,092 --> 00:06:37,049
<i>Let the gun aim only at me.</i>

62
00:06:46,028 --> 00:06:47,749
Keep a close watch on the surroundings.

63
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:06,740
Honey...

64
00:07:07,976 --> 00:07:09,676
Honey!

65
00:07:15,448 --> 00:07:17,683
Honey, what do I do?

66
00:07:20,836 --> 00:07:22,096
<i>What do I do? Honey...</i>

67
00:07:22,096 --> 00:07:23,796
Ms. Yoo.

68
00:07:33,148 --> 00:07:36,249
It's you, Layla.

69
00:07:37,792 --> 00:07:39,616
Let's get her.

70
00:07:50,688 --> 00:07:52,268
<i>She's not inside the building.</i>

71
00:07:52,268 --> 00:07:53,968
<i>She's not here either.</i>

72
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:02,784
<i>Northern end of the park.</i>

73
00:08:02,784 --> 00:08:04,683
<i>Suspect spotted near the Han River area.</i>

74
00:08:04,683 --> 00:08:06,772
She's heading toward Seonyu Bridge.

75
00:08:06,772 --> 00:08:08,272
Everyone, move that way!

76
00:08:08,272 --> 00:08:09,983
Darn it.

77
00:08:37,993 --> 00:08:40,183
Let's get out of here first.

78
00:09:06,346 --> 00:09:09,124
Suspect spotted. The suspect
is armed with what appears to be a firearm.

79
00:09:09,124 --> 00:09:11,183
Secure her before she leaves the park.

80
00:09:35,404 --> 00:09:38,496
[No Entry]

81
00:09:44,052 --> 00:09:47,892
We're the ones who should be thanking you
for inviting us into your home.

82
00:09:50,324 --> 00:09:51,660
Look how we meet.

83
00:09:51,660 --> 00:09:53,360
Come with me.

84
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:59,540
This way.

85
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:02,483
Watch your step. It's slippery.

86
00:10:22,392 --> 00:10:25,832
Kwon Tae Seong seems to have made his choice.

87
00:10:25,832 --> 00:10:27,849
Now, it's Yoo Bo Na's turn.

88
00:10:38,188 --> 00:10:39,888
Freeze!

89
00:10:40,722 --> 00:10:42,422
Police!

90
00:10:53,784 --> 00:10:56,032
Drop your weapon and put your hands up!

91
00:10:56,032 --> 00:10:57,732
Hurry!

92
00:10:58,668 --> 00:11:00,783
It's all over now, Kingfisher.

93
00:11:01,796 --> 00:11:03,496
Drop the gun.

94
00:11:05,112 --> 00:11:06,983
Kingfisher?

95
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:10,360
Yoo Bo Na...

96
00:11:12,144 --> 00:11:15,216
You're darn lucky.

97
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:16,983
Darn it.

98
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:34,949
Ceasefire!

99
00:11:35,992 --> 00:11:37,816
Ceasefire!

100
00:12:11,616 --> 00:12:15,449
As you know, we can't take her
to a regular hospital.

101
00:12:17,172 --> 00:12:18,872
Okay.

102
00:12:41,816 --> 00:12:43,516
Take her inside.

103
00:12:45,301 --> 00:12:46,784
Director Yoo!

104
00:12:46,784 --> 00:12:49,016
Get ready, hurry.

105
00:12:51,672 --> 00:12:53,383
She'll be all right.

106
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,980
[No Entry]

107
00:12:59,168 --> 00:13:00,868
Tae Seong.

108
00:13:01,552 --> 00:13:06,004
There are people who help
where they're needed.

109
00:13:06,004 --> 00:13:07,704
She's going to be okay.

110
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:10,500
Okay.

111
00:13:20,824 --> 00:13:22,868
[Operating Room]

112
00:13:52,044 --> 00:13:53,744
Have a seat.

113
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:18,232
Luckily, only the muscle was damaged.
The vital organs were unharmed.

114
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:21,616
She'll be fine with some rest.

115
00:14:22,808 --> 00:14:24,508
Thank you.

116
00:14:34,112 --> 00:14:35,812
Mr. Lee!

117
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,800
The NFS team is all standing by.

118
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:42,983
It's a serious case, so the director
will conduct the autopsy personally.

119
00:14:42,983 --> 00:14:45,584
Man, we'll be up all night
if we're doing an autopsy, then.

120
00:14:45,584 --> 00:14:47,812
Anything unusual
while you were keeping watch?

121
00:14:47,812 --> 00:14:50,012
Any suspicious activity?

122
00:14:50,012 --> 00:14:51,384
No, nothing in particular.

123
00:14:51,384 --> 00:14:53,516
Is something bothering you?

124
00:14:55,149 --> 00:15:00,583
I don't know what I missed
or what I'm missing.

125
00:15:08,912 --> 00:15:10,649
Why did you do it?

126
00:15:12,076 --> 00:15:13,776
Huh?

127
00:15:15,032 --> 00:15:18,116
Why did you take the bullet for me...

128
00:15:20,288 --> 00:15:22,592
How am I supposed to live

129
00:15:22,592 --> 00:15:25,049
if something happens to you?

130
00:15:27,008 --> 00:15:31,716
Without you... how am I supposed to live?

131
00:16:08,883 --> 00:16:11,216
[Chief Na Guk Jin]

132
00:16:11,983 --> 00:16:13,716
[Decline]

133
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:24,016
<i>Hey, Kwon Tae Seong,
why aren't you answering?</i>

134
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:25,208
<i>Don't tell me you're still asleep?</i>

135
00:16:25,208 --> 00:16:27,812
<i>Kingfisher was shot
and killed by the police last night.</i>

136
00:16:27,812 --> 00:16:30,316
<i>Hey, get over there. The NFS or
the police headquarters, wherever.</i>

137
00:16:30,316 --> 00:16:31,372
[Breaking News: Kingfisher Killed by Police]

138
00:16:31,372 --> 00:16:35,916
<i>Serial sniper Kingfisher
was killed last night.</i>

139
00:16:35,916 --> 00:16:38,749
<i>Enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.</i>

140
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:46,148
<i>According to reports,
Kingfisher was shot and killed</i>

141
00:16:46,148 --> 00:16:49,083
<i>after a chase with police at an undisclosed
location in Seoul last night.</i>

142
00:16:49,083 --> 00:16:52,116
<i>Kingfisher's identity, which had
remained a mystery for 15 years,</i>

143
00:16:52,116 --> 00:16:54,288
<i>has unexpectedly been revealed
to be a woman in her 30s.</i>

144
00:16:54,288 --> 00:16:57,149
<i>The revelation has shocked
and confused the public.</i>

145
00:16:57,149 --> 00:16:58,149
You're from the NFS, right?

146
00:16:58,149 --> 00:16:59,672
Has Kingfisher's identity been confirmed?

147
00:16:59,672 --> 00:17:01,588
Who is she? Please release
her name and photo.

148
00:17:01,588 --> 00:17:03,116
Why was she killed instead of taken alive?

149
00:17:03,116 --> 00:17:06,149
Are you certain the woman in her 30s
who died at the scene was Kingfisher?

150
00:17:06,149 --> 00:17:07,783
Was there any excessive
use of force by the police?

151
00:17:07,783 --> 00:17:10,516
Will we never know Kingfisher's motive?

152
00:17:12,604 --> 00:17:13,740
Finally got her.

153
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:16,812
Good work.

154
00:17:16,812 --> 00:17:18,916
Finally got her.

155
00:17:22,896 --> 00:17:24,908
Good job.

156
00:17:24,908 --> 00:17:26,732
But what do you mean we can't identify her?

157
00:17:26,732 --> 00:17:30,544
Her fingerprints and DNA don't match
anything in our national databases.

158
00:17:30,544 --> 00:17:33,048
We checked with Immigration as well,

159
00:17:33,048 --> 00:17:35,524
but there are no matching fingerprints
from any foreign national.

160
00:17:35,524 --> 00:17:38,232
So what, did she enter the country illegally?

161
00:17:38,232 --> 00:17:43,083
We've requested an identity check
through Interpol channels for now.

162
00:17:43,083 --> 00:17:44,083
Oh, man.

163
00:17:44,083 --> 00:17:46,572
Nothing about this is ever straightforward.

164
00:17:46,572 --> 00:17:49,149
Still, at least we've got her.

165
00:17:49,824 --> 00:17:51,216
Well done.

166
00:17:51,216 --> 00:17:52,916
Good work.

167
00:17:54,183 --> 00:17:56,636
[Commissioner General]

168
00:17:56,636 --> 00:17:58,956
Calls are blowing up everywhere.

169
00:17:58,956 --> 00:18:00,656
Yes, Commissioner.

170
00:18:29,149 --> 00:18:30,849
Honey!

171
00:18:32,188 --> 00:18:33,976
Are you okay?

172
00:18:33,976 --> 00:18:36,060
Are you all right?

173
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:37,784
You've been through so much.

174
00:18:37,784 --> 00:18:40,536
Does anything hurt? Any discomfort?

175
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:42,883
Should I get the doctor?

176
00:18:46,468 --> 00:18:48,583
Honey, if you get up now...

177
00:18:53,996 --> 00:18:56,583
Could you get the team leader for me?

178
00:18:59,448 --> 00:19:01,148
Okay.

179
00:19:06,344 --> 00:19:09,828
Is Director Yoo okay? Is she awake?

180
00:19:09,828 --> 00:19:11,528
Yes.

181
00:19:14,944 --> 00:19:17,949
Team Leader, Bo Na's looking for you.

182
00:19:30,744 --> 00:19:33,992
Yeah, Se Ah. I don't think
I can make it home today.

183
00:19:33,992 --> 00:19:37,104
<i>Alright. I'll have her sleep over
at my place tonight.</i>

184
00:19:37,104 --> 00:19:38,804
Please take care of her.

185
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,700
Honey, what are you doing?

186
00:19:53,664 --> 00:19:55,516
Why? Where are you going?

187
00:19:57,418 --> 00:20:00,649
You already knew, didn't you?

188
00:20:03,008 --> 00:20:04,349
It was from that day on.

189
00:20:04,349 --> 00:20:06,816
The day Yul went to the ER.

190
00:20:06,816 --> 00:20:09,149
You kept avoiding my eyes,

191
00:20:09,988 --> 00:20:12,916
looking at me like I was a stranger.

192
00:20:18,904 --> 00:20:21,583
That's why you came home late for a while

193
00:20:21,583 --> 00:20:24,749
and couldn't eat or sleep properly.

194
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,900
- Honey, I...
- That must have been tough for you.

195
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,552
Honey, just hear me out for a second.

196
00:20:29,552 --> 00:20:31,349
You were angry, too, weren't you?

197
00:20:31,349 --> 00:20:35,444
At the wife who's been lying
to you all this time, weren't you?

198
00:20:37,216 --> 00:20:39,484
You must've been

199
00:20:39,484 --> 00:20:41,716
confused and lost.

200
00:20:45,104 --> 00:20:46,804
I was.

201
00:20:49,856 --> 00:20:52,072
I was angry,

202
00:20:52,072 --> 00:20:54,349
confused, and completely lost.

203
00:20:55,144 --> 00:20:58,320
Honestly, your secret was
too much for me. I was scared.

204
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,849
But...

205
00:20:59,849 --> 00:21:02,683
I've come to one conclusion. To protect you.

206
00:21:04,016 --> 00:21:07,216
To protect you and our family.

207
00:21:09,148 --> 00:21:11,696
Honey, can't we just go back to how we were?

208
00:21:11,696 --> 00:21:13,396
We can smile again

209
00:21:15,364 --> 00:21:18,049
and act like nothing ever happened.

210
00:21:21,192 --> 00:21:23,449
Pretend none of this happened?

211
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:34,016
I don't think I can do that.

212
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:43,184
Every time you look at me,
you'll think about who I really am.

213
00:21:43,184 --> 00:21:47,049
You'll find me strange,
and you'll be confused and in pain.

214
00:21:50,849 --> 00:21:54,424
You'll be constantly wondering
when everything's going to blow up.

215
00:21:54,424 --> 00:21:57,049
No. That's not going to happen.

216
00:21:57,049 --> 00:21:58,644
I'll become your living hell.

217
00:21:58,644 --> 00:22:00,016
No, honey.

218
00:22:00,016 --> 00:22:02,416
No, please don't do this...

219
00:22:10,268 --> 00:22:12,416
I can't go back to the way things were.

220
00:22:15,580 --> 00:22:18,149
You still don't truly know me.

221
00:22:52,784 --> 00:22:54,004
Honey!

222
00:22:54,004 --> 00:22:56,223
Honey, wait...

223
00:22:56,223 --> 00:22:57,923
Honey!

224
00:24:00,320 --> 00:24:02,520
<i>I can't go back to the way things were.</i>

225
00:24:02,520 --> 00:24:04,696
<i>You still don't truly know me.</i>

226
00:24:04,696 --> 00:24:08,380
Director Yoo has submitted her resignation.

227
00:24:08,380 --> 00:24:11,096
We suggested sick leave
or a leave of absence,

228
00:24:11,096 --> 00:24:13,516
but I think she's made up her mind.

229
00:24:34,928 --> 00:24:36,628
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

230
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:44,648
I stopped by on my way to the airport.

231
00:24:44,648 --> 00:24:46,784
I'm sorry.

232
00:24:46,784 --> 00:24:49,408
I should've acted sooner.

233
00:24:49,408 --> 00:24:52,016
Could that gunshot have...

234
00:24:53,268 --> 00:24:56,068
Mama sent me to protect her.

235
00:24:56,068 --> 00:24:58,916
I'm probably going to get an earful
from her when I get back.

236
00:25:01,224 --> 00:25:03,883
Is Bo Na going with you?

237
00:25:08,168 --> 00:25:10,508
I know from experience.

238
00:25:10,508 --> 00:25:13,872
Just mentioning her husband or child

239
00:25:13,872 --> 00:25:16,780
makes Yoo Bo Na's eyes go wild.

240
00:25:16,780 --> 00:25:18,504
For someone like that...

241
00:25:18,504 --> 00:25:21,649
I asked her a few times, just in case,

242
00:25:21,649 --> 00:25:23,744
but she flat-out refused.

243
00:25:23,744 --> 00:25:26,116
She'd disappoint the person waiting for her.

244
00:25:31,432 --> 00:25:34,884
I meant it when I said Bo Na seemed

245
00:25:34,884 --> 00:25:36,908
to have found a good guy.

246
00:25:36,908 --> 00:25:39,548
I told her the same thing.

247
00:25:39,548 --> 00:25:43,988
Well, she probably knows that
better than anyone.

248
00:25:43,988 --> 00:25:45,688
So...

249
00:25:52,836 --> 00:25:54,536
Thank you.

250
00:26:09,024 --> 00:26:11,049
Please take care of it.

251
00:26:31,172 --> 00:26:34,149
I sent these flowers to Cheol today.

252
00:26:34,149 --> 00:26:36,156
They're called marguerites.

253
00:26:36,156 --> 00:26:38,440
They look a lot like
cosmos flowers, don't they?

254
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:41,960
So customers often confuse them.

255
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:44,516
What is their flower language?

256
00:26:45,816 --> 00:26:48,012
"Revealing a secret."

257
00:26:48,012 --> 00:26:49,940
"True love."

258
00:26:49,940 --> 00:26:52,716
"True love has no secrets."

259
00:26:52,716 --> 00:26:55,649
"True love means revealing the truth."

260
00:26:56,344 --> 00:26:58,616
That's what I thought it meant.

261
00:26:58,616 --> 00:27:02,796
But someone told me that
the meaning wasn't very nice.

262
00:27:02,796 --> 00:27:06,216
Sometimes you keep secrets
because you love someone too much.

263
00:27:07,404 --> 00:27:10,084
<i>He's someone who lives in the light.</i>

264
00:27:10,084 --> 00:27:12,383
<i>Because he's different from me.</i>

265
00:27:12,992 --> 00:27:16,816
Because if he knew how different we are,
we couldn't stay together.

266
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:20,668
I'm not worried.

267
00:27:20,668 --> 00:27:22,516
Because that day will never come.

268
00:27:23,812 --> 00:27:27,016
Because the day he sees my other side

269
00:27:27,784 --> 00:27:29,783
will never come.

270
00:27:30,483 --> 00:27:32,876
<i>Back then, I thought it was confidence</i>

271
00:27:32,876 --> 00:27:35,016
that she'd never
let her secret be discovered,

272
00:27:35,016 --> 00:27:39,216
but thinking about it now,
I think it was anxiety.

273
00:27:41,568 --> 00:27:45,940
A promise she was making
to herself not to be afraid.

274
00:27:45,940 --> 00:27:50,816
Because she already knew how it would end.

275
00:27:52,844 --> 00:27:55,584
Maybe she'd already decided

276
00:27:55,584 --> 00:27:59,092
from the beginning how this would end

277
00:27:59,092 --> 00:28:01,849
when the moment came.

278
00:28:04,116 --> 00:28:06,949
That's what I've come to think.

279
00:28:14,383 --> 00:28:17,649
[Forensic DNA profile comparison]

280
00:28:21,364 --> 00:28:23,583
Kingfisher Task Force.

281
00:28:25,048 --> 00:28:26,749
Oh, yes.

282
00:28:27,984 --> 00:28:30,052
Did we hear back from Interpol?

283
00:28:30,052 --> 00:28:31,949
Yes, thank you.

284
00:28:33,416 --> 00:28:35,583
Mr. Lee, International Cooperation says

285
00:28:35,583 --> 00:28:39,316
they found a DNA match
for the body found in Russia.

286
00:28:39,316 --> 00:28:40,316
Russia?

287
00:28:40,316 --> 00:28:42,924
[DNA Match Search Against
Russian Federation Records]

288
00:28:42,924 --> 00:28:46,216
"Layla Choi, age 38."

289
00:28:46,216 --> 00:28:48,552
"Reported missing approximately
15 years ago."

290
00:28:48,552 --> 00:28:50,788
"No record of her whereabouts since?"

291
00:28:50,788 --> 00:28:54,756
Fifteen years... That lines up with
Kingfisher's active period, right?

292
00:28:54,756 --> 00:28:56,820
Man, then that's pretty conclusive.

293
00:28:56,820 --> 00:28:58,649
So her name was Layla?

294
00:28:58,649 --> 00:29:01,572
So she must have entered illegally
15 years ago

295
00:29:01,572 --> 00:29:03,916
and lived as an undocumented resident.

296
00:29:07,649 --> 00:29:09,732
Doesn't something feel off?

297
00:29:09,732 --> 00:29:11,592
What do you mean?

298
00:29:11,592 --> 00:29:14,856
Oh, you mean the other DNA from the hair?

299
00:29:14,856 --> 00:29:18,292
Well, that could've
belonged to an accomplice.

300
00:29:18,292 --> 00:29:24,249
But why would she go to that park alone
in the middle of the night?

301
00:29:25,508 --> 00:29:27,472
Exactly.

302
00:29:27,472 --> 00:29:29,716
Maybe she went there to meet someone?

303
00:29:29,716 --> 00:29:32,884
But the park was closed at that hour.
There shouldn't have been anyone there.

304
00:29:32,884 --> 00:29:34,584
You're right.

305
00:29:36,032 --> 00:29:38,683
There shouldn't have been anyone.

306
00:29:42,772 --> 00:29:44,816
Oh, you're here?

307
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:45,844
Yeah, where's Yul?

308
00:29:45,844 --> 00:29:47,956
She's already asleep. Look at the time.

309
00:29:47,956 --> 00:29:49,883
Let her sleep here tonight.

310
00:29:50,924 --> 00:29:52,624
Mom...

311
00:30:02,692 --> 00:30:05,749
Where's Yul's mom?

312
00:30:06,864 --> 00:30:09,912
I told you. She's away on
a long-term business trip overseas.

313
00:30:09,912 --> 00:30:11,096
All of a sudden?

314
00:30:11,096 --> 00:30:12,320
Where overseas?

315
00:30:12,320 --> 00:30:14,176
When's she coming back?

316
00:30:14,176 --> 00:30:16,764
Look at that guilty look on his face.

317
00:30:16,764 --> 00:30:18,160
He's terrible at lying.

318
00:30:18,160 --> 00:30:19,719
I knew something was wrong

319
00:30:19,719 --> 00:30:22,423
when he came home
looking so pale and worn out.

320
00:30:22,423 --> 00:30:26,164
Tell me. What on earth did you do to Bo Na?

321
00:30:26,164 --> 00:30:28,008
- Huh?
- Huh?

322
00:30:28,008 --> 00:30:30,820
Did you throw a tantrum because she
put her job before you and the kid?

323
00:30:30,820 --> 00:30:33,740
What kind of world do you think this is?

324
00:30:33,740 --> 00:30:35,232
He still hasn't come to his senses.

325
00:30:35,232 --> 00:30:37,256
I definitely think
you're the one who messed up.

326
00:30:37,256 --> 00:30:38,740
Exactly. That's what I'm saying!

327
00:30:38,740 --> 00:30:40,828
When she first got married,

328
00:30:40,828 --> 00:30:43,816
I gave her a hard time
for being bad with a knife,

329
00:30:43,816 --> 00:30:46,208
and a month later, she showed up
with calluses on her hands.

330
00:30:46,208 --> 00:30:48,244
She must've chopped enough
to wear her hands out.

331
00:30:48,244 --> 00:30:50,368
Back then, she didn't even know
who Hyun Bin was, so I gave her a weird look.

332
00:30:50,368 --> 00:30:53,048
Then she watched everything he was in
and came back reciting his lines.

333
00:30:53,048 --> 00:30:55,948
"Sun Il, I'm not weird anymore, right?"

334
00:30:55,948 --> 00:30:57,404
Even though I never asked her to,

335
00:30:57,404 --> 00:31:00,416
she got life, accident, indemnity,
and dementia insurance

336
00:31:00,416 --> 00:31:03,016
for everyone in her department.

337
00:31:03,016 --> 00:31:04,760
I was top of the sales rankings that month.

338
00:31:04,760 --> 00:31:05,852
- No way!
- Seriously?

339
00:31:05,852 --> 00:31:07,220
Yeah.

340
00:31:07,220 --> 00:31:09,564
That's just the kind of person she is. Okay?

341
00:31:09,564 --> 00:31:12,492
She works herself to the bone
for everything! Okay?

342
00:31:12,492 --> 00:31:14,516
How bad could it have been

343
00:31:14,516 --> 00:31:19,616
for someone so devoted to her family
to leave even Yul behind?

344
00:31:19,616 --> 00:31:23,816
She doesn't have any friends,
so she probably has nowhere to go, either.

345
00:31:25,308 --> 00:31:29,608
Does she have parents
to go back to? Any family?

346
00:31:29,608 --> 00:31:33,340
She has nowhere in this world to go.

347
00:31:33,340 --> 00:31:37,583
What on earth did you do
to make her leave her own home?

348
00:31:38,505 --> 00:31:41,304
Oh, gosh.

349
00:31:41,304 --> 00:31:42,849
- Huh?
- Mom!

350
00:31:42,849 --> 00:31:44,454
- Are you okay?
- Careful.

351
00:31:44,454 --> 00:31:46,232
Mom, your blood pressure's going up.

352
00:31:46,232 --> 00:31:47,448
- Let me see.
- Oh, Mom!

353
00:31:47,448 --> 00:31:49,750
- Bring it down.
- You can't let your blood pressure go up.

354
00:31:49,750 --> 00:31:50,969
Her blood pressure shouldn't go up.
Go buy medicine!

355
00:31:50,969 --> 00:31:51,983
- Quick.
- Quick, get a calming pill.

356
00:31:51,983 --> 00:31:53,512
Mom! Mom, are you okay?

357
00:31:53,512 --> 00:31:57,252
It breaks my heart just thinking about it...

358
00:31:57,252 --> 00:31:59,112
My wife has a lot of people on her side.

359
00:31:59,112 --> 00:32:02,112
Oh, my. Jeez.

360
00:32:11,031 --> 00:32:12,583
<i>She doesn't have any family here.</i>

361
00:32:12,583 --> 00:32:15,000
[Eight Years Ago]

362
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:17,160
She was adopted by
a Russian family as a child

363
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:19,649
and came back as an adult.

364
00:32:27,064 --> 00:32:29,724
Please look out for my girlfriend.

365
00:32:29,724 --> 00:32:32,160
Why are you asking me?

366
00:32:32,160 --> 00:32:33,883
You're the one who needs to treat her right.

367
00:32:36,144 --> 00:32:38,316
You said she has no family.

368
00:32:39,236 --> 00:32:41,183
So you take good care of her, buddy.

369
00:32:51,140 --> 00:32:52,840
<i>Suspect spotted.</i>

370
00:33:02,176 --> 00:33:04,349
[Headband, Red Devil, Tall and Slender]

371
00:33:05,883 --> 00:33:08,316
[Short or Tied Hair, Big Bag on Shoulder]

372
00:33:12,300 --> 00:33:14,033
<i>My wife and my child.</i>

373
00:33:14,033 --> 00:33:15,949
My beloved family.

374
00:33:16,792 --> 00:33:18,312
I need to protect them.

375
00:33:18,312 --> 00:33:20,216
You'll be on my side, right?

376
00:33:21,300 --> 00:33:23,116
<i>You said you wanted to repay the favor.</i>

377
00:33:33,649 --> 00:33:36,216
[Not Today]

378
00:33:41,512 --> 00:33:44,000
It must've really shaken him.

379
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:47,099
He's been completely out of it ever since.

380
00:33:47,099 --> 00:33:52,624
I know. He's been reading nothing
but Kingfisher articles all day.

381
00:33:52,624 --> 00:33:55,249
Maybe he was shocked
to find out she was a woman?

382
00:33:55,249 --> 00:33:59,616
Or is he upset that he missed the scoop?

383
00:34:00,508 --> 00:34:05,016
Well, he must be feeling pretty torn
after looking into it for so long.

384
00:34:05,016 --> 00:34:07,360
Reporters get like that sometimes.

385
00:34:07,360 --> 00:34:09,716
Leave him alone for a while.

386
00:34:09,716 --> 00:34:13,683
[Killed by a Gun, Dead by a Gun:
Kingfisher's Miserable End]

387
00:34:14,916 --> 00:34:18,516
[From Champion of Justice to Brutal Killer:
Kingfisher's Downfall]

388
00:34:19,968 --> 00:34:22,136
I opened the door to serve food in the room,

389
00:34:22,136 --> 00:34:25,292
and the two of them
suddenly stopped whispering.

390
00:34:25,292 --> 00:34:29,220
I got curious, so I stepped outside
and listened through the crack in the door.

391
00:34:29,220 --> 00:34:32,622
"Let's do it abroad. We'll meet there."

392
00:34:32,622 --> 00:34:34,748
They said something like that.

393
00:34:34,748 --> 00:34:38,483
Did you hear what they were planning to do?

394
00:34:39,424 --> 00:34:42,016
I think they mentioned some girl.

395
00:34:42,700 --> 00:34:46,749
Oh, and that it could all be done for money
with no strings attached.

396
00:35:02,044 --> 00:35:04,032
Oh.

397
00:35:04,032 --> 00:35:06,272
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong.

398
00:35:06,272 --> 00:35:09,149
Good to see you. Please come in.

399
00:35:15,064 --> 00:35:19,744
In the past, Director Yoo
said she wanted to quit.

400
00:35:19,744 --> 00:35:21,900
We all tried to talk her out of it.

401
00:35:21,900 --> 00:35:24,372
Because everyone worried that

402
00:35:24,372 --> 00:35:27,772
she might literally die
if she kept going like that.

403
00:35:27,772 --> 00:35:29,483
Director Yoo kept

404
00:35:30,740 --> 00:35:32,749
moving forward

405
00:35:33,849 --> 00:35:35,683
with one thing in mind.

406
00:35:36,816 --> 00:35:38,649
She believed that if she kept at it,

407
00:35:39,916 --> 00:35:42,748
the world would get a little better.

408
00:35:42,748 --> 00:35:43,992
A little safer.

409
00:35:43,992 --> 00:35:45,716
But...

410
00:35:46,392 --> 00:35:49,183
does the world really get better that easily?

411
00:35:49,936 --> 00:35:56,416
That's what made Director Yoo
the most exhausted and worn out.

412
00:36:00,876 --> 00:36:03,600
Huh? Hold on! Wait!

413
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:06,349
We made her take an extended leave

414
00:36:07,264 --> 00:36:10,004
to give her some time
to get her life back on track.

415
00:36:10,004 --> 00:36:11,704
If she still felt the same

416
00:36:12,512 --> 00:36:16,984
after she came back,
we promised we wouldn't try to stop her.

417
00:36:16,984 --> 00:36:19,296
But three or four months later,

418
00:36:19,296 --> 00:36:23,849
she came back and asked us
to tear up her resignation.

419
00:36:34,592 --> 00:36:39,349
I think Director Yoo still needs
that kind of time right now.

420
00:36:40,088 --> 00:36:45,283
So think of it as giving her a long trip.

421
00:36:46,012 --> 00:36:51,016
And maybe, just like when the two of you
first met at a desperate time,

422
00:36:51,756 --> 00:36:54,383
another chance will come

423
00:36:55,672 --> 00:36:58,349
<i>when you need each other just as badly.</i>

424
00:37:06,949 --> 00:37:08,916
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

425
00:37:16,208 --> 00:37:17,852
What's up this late?

426
00:37:17,852 --> 00:37:21,120
<i>Well, just thought of you.</i>

427
00:37:21,120 --> 00:37:23,108
<i>What are you doing?</i>

428
00:37:23,108 --> 00:37:26,184
My wife and Yul wanted ice cream,

429
00:37:26,184 --> 00:37:28,232
so I went to the convenience store.
I'm heading home now.

430
00:37:28,232 --> 00:37:29,424
Ice cream?

431
00:37:29,424 --> 00:37:31,124
At this hour?

432
00:37:31,824 --> 00:37:33,649
They wanted some.

433
00:37:35,708 --> 00:37:38,684
Then evening training will be tough
while you're looking after Yul.

434
00:37:38,684 --> 00:37:40,849
Alright, keep in touch.

435
00:37:42,408 --> 00:37:43,512
What about Yul?

436
00:37:43,512 --> 00:37:45,782
Well, Se Ah's sister-in-law went somewhere,

437
00:37:45,782 --> 00:37:47,544
so she's staying at Se Ah's for a while.

438
00:37:47,544 --> 00:37:50,220
Ms. Bo Na? Where did she go?

439
00:37:50,220 --> 00:37:53,050
Her brother says she went on
a long business trip overseas,

440
00:37:53,050 --> 00:37:54,949
but Se Ah isn't so sure.

441
00:37:54,949 --> 00:37:56,859
Maybe something happened between them.

442
00:37:56,859 --> 00:37:59,149
<i>Things haven't seemed great at home lately.</i>

443
00:38:00,764 --> 00:38:02,464
Hello?

444
00:38:04,187 --> 00:38:06,272
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]
Why call and say nothing?

445
00:38:06,272 --> 00:38:08,936
Hello? Lee Dong Jin!

446
00:38:08,936 --> 00:38:10,892
You...

447
00:38:10,892 --> 00:38:12,544
I'm going to ask you one important question,

448
00:38:12,544 --> 00:38:15,183
so think carefully before you answer.

449
00:38:17,508 --> 00:38:19,192
What now? What is it?

450
00:38:19,192 --> 00:38:22,260
Who do you like more, me or your wife?

451
00:38:22,260 --> 00:38:23,960
You crazy punk, are you drunk?

452
00:38:23,960 --> 00:38:25,220
<i>I'm serious right now.</i>

453
00:38:25,220 --> 00:38:27,828
Of course, I love my Bo Na.

454
00:38:27,828 --> 00:38:30,392
I could live just fine without you
for a thousand years.

455
00:38:30,392 --> 00:38:33,692
But I couldn't live a single day
without my Bo Na.

456
00:38:33,692 --> 00:38:36,249
You mean that? Really?

457
00:38:36,249 --> 00:38:37,849
You don't regret it, right?

458
00:38:37,849 --> 00:38:39,000
<i>No.</i>

459
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:41,683
Ask me a hundred times.
My answer won't change.

460
00:38:43,883 --> 00:38:48,649
The best thing I ever did
was meet Bo Na, marry her...

461
00:38:50,208 --> 00:38:52,083
and start a family.

462
00:38:59,260 --> 00:39:01,283
Ugh, hang up, you crazy punk!

463
00:39:45,349 --> 00:39:48,116
[Mommy, I miss you. I love you so much]

464
00:39:52,484 --> 00:39:54,724
<i>Which one did you like best?</i>

465
00:39:54,724 --> 00:39:58,416
<i>Well... I loved them all.
I loved every moment.</i>

466
00:39:58,416 --> 00:39:59,644
[Six Years Ago, Summer]

467
00:39:59,644 --> 00:40:01,151
- This is so nice!
- There are so many

468
00:40:01,151 --> 00:40:02,949
- pretty things over there.
- Here?

469
00:40:03,732 --> 00:40:06,383
Okay, one, two!

470
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:11,336
Stand here.

471
00:40:11,336 --> 00:40:13,584
Me?

472
00:40:13,584 --> 00:40:14,968
- Princess Yoo Bo Na!
- What?

473
00:40:14,968 --> 00:40:17,056
Stay classy.

474
00:40:17,056 --> 00:40:18,544
- It's dangerous, right?
- Yeah.

475
00:40:18,544 --> 00:40:20,128
Strike a pose.

476
00:40:20,128 --> 00:40:23,276
One, two, three!

477
00:40:23,276 --> 00:40:25,592
Take a picture in a beautiful setting.

478
00:40:25,592 --> 00:40:27,592
Did we complete today's mission?

479
00:40:27,592 --> 00:40:30,083
- Mission complete!
- Okay, great.

480
00:40:30,704 --> 00:40:31,995
What should we do next?

481
00:40:31,995 --> 00:40:35,208
Next? Well...

482
00:40:35,208 --> 00:40:40,184
Oh! How about making jjajang ramyeon
at home on Sunday?

483
00:40:40,184 --> 00:40:43,046
You know, the Sunday jjajang ramyeon chef.

484
00:40:43,046 --> 00:40:44,200
Please make that for me.

485
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:45,208
Alright.

486
00:40:45,208 --> 00:40:46,416
- What else?
- Well...

487
00:40:46,416 --> 00:40:48,988
- Having strawberry shakes for dessert!
- Okay.

488
00:40:48,988 --> 00:40:50,680
Watching a late-night movie. A horror movie.

489
00:40:50,680 --> 00:40:51,949
- Oh, sounds good!
- How about that?

490
00:40:51,949 --> 00:40:54,528
- You can handle that, right?
- No.

491
00:40:54,528 --> 00:40:58,164
Then we'll have a picnic
by the Han River and eat fried chicken.

492
00:40:58,164 --> 00:40:59,583
We've got so much to do.

493
00:40:59,583 --> 00:41:01,028
We'd better get busy, then.

494
00:41:01,028 --> 00:41:02,620
Tae Seong, is there anything you want to do?

495
00:41:02,620 --> 00:41:04,320
I want to get married.

496
00:41:07,524 --> 00:41:10,568
Marriage is a bit early for you, huh?

497
00:41:10,568 --> 00:41:12,268
Oh...

498
00:41:16,083 --> 00:41:19,708
But when people do this, don't they...

499
00:41:19,708 --> 00:41:22,396
do it while giving something?

500
00:41:22,396 --> 00:41:24,512
This is a proposal, right?

501
00:41:24,512 --> 00:41:25,704
On TV, when people do this,

502
00:41:25,704 --> 00:41:28,032
- they always give something.
- Oh, well...

503
00:41:28,032 --> 00:41:29,384
Oh, I mean...

504
00:41:29,384 --> 00:41:32,256
This isn't an official proposal.

505
00:41:32,256 --> 00:41:36,048
It's just that everything I'd been
keeping bottled up inside...

506
00:41:36,048 --> 00:41:37,189
It just came spilling out.

507
00:41:37,189 --> 00:41:39,536
But I was planning
to make a proper proposal...

508
00:41:39,536 --> 00:41:43,120
I had a ring all ready to give you...

509
00:41:43,120 --> 00:41:44,820
Okay.

510
00:41:48,372 --> 00:41:49,976
But...

511
00:41:49,976 --> 00:41:51,676
Well...

512
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:54,416
When are you going to do it?

513
00:41:56,288 --> 00:41:58,856
Once you've picked a date,
let me know beforehand.

514
00:41:58,856 --> 00:42:03,960
That way, I can think about
what I'm going to say.

515
00:42:03,960 --> 00:42:06,149
Be sure to tell me the date.

516
00:42:12,576 --> 00:42:14,749
Tae Seong, come on.

517
00:42:20,924 --> 00:42:24,284
<i>There's still so much I want to do with you.</i>

518
00:42:24,284 --> 00:42:25,284
Really?

519
00:42:25,284 --> 00:42:30,848
Something we haven't done before.
Something better and more special.

520
00:42:30,848 --> 00:42:35,056
Let's do every single one of them together.

521
00:42:35,056 --> 00:42:37,048
Yeah.

522
00:42:37,048 --> 00:42:38,748
Together.

523
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:23,828
Mr. Kwon!

524
00:43:23,828 --> 00:43:26,752
Your hunch was right.

525
00:43:26,752 --> 00:43:29,942
The two Kingfisher victims
were both in Cambodia

526
00:43:29,942 --> 00:43:31,960
[Booking Information]
around the same time last summer.

527
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:34,149
And this.

528
00:43:34,149 --> 00:43:37,628
And during that time, a mom
and daughter selling food on the street

529
00:43:37,628 --> 00:43:40,052
were murdered in Cambodia.

530
00:43:40,052 --> 00:43:42,716
Their bodies were found,

531
00:43:43,424 --> 00:43:45,200
but the killer was never caught?

532
00:43:45,200 --> 00:43:47,824
Please prepare a travel request.
Four days and three nights in Cambodia.

533
00:43:47,824 --> 00:43:49,849
Okay, understood.

534
00:43:51,383 --> 00:43:53,449
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

535
00:43:56,492 --> 00:43:58,812
Detective Lee Dong Jin,

536
00:43:58,812 --> 00:44:02,949
let's wrap up this case properly together.

537
00:44:12,916 --> 00:44:15,456
- Darn it.
- Kwon Se Ah, you've still got it.

538
00:44:15,456 --> 00:44:17,983
Of course, I'll be looking sharp
as a cop soon too.

539
00:44:17,983 --> 00:44:20,292
Come on. You're taking
the police too lightly.

540
00:44:20,292 --> 00:44:23,072
It is easy. Even a guy
who got thrown by a tiny girl

541
00:44:23,072 --> 00:44:25,892
and whined to keep it a secret is a cop now.

542
00:44:25,892 --> 00:44:27,749
How long are you going to bring that up...

543
00:44:30,784 --> 00:44:32,220
Hey, that's a cheap move!

544
00:44:32,220 --> 00:44:34,316
That's why you need to focus.

545
00:44:41,600 --> 00:44:43,168
That was dangerous just now.
Stay focused, okay?

546
00:44:43,168 --> 00:44:45,136
Darn it. I told you not to go easy on me!

547
00:44:45,136 --> 00:44:46,849
Are you going to do judo with your mouth?

548
00:45:04,616 --> 00:45:07,616
Oh!

549
00:45:13,916 --> 00:45:17,316
Ugh, I almost died doing judo.

550
00:45:18,516 --> 00:45:20,700
Hey, this is exactly why I told you not to.

551
00:45:20,700 --> 00:45:22,883
What are you doing in a sacred judo gym?

552
00:45:22,883 --> 00:45:23,883
Hey, what did I do?

553
00:45:23,883 --> 00:45:25,883
What are you doing?
This is a judo gym, not a wrestling ring.

554
00:45:25,883 --> 00:45:28,116
You went easy on me, didn't you?

555
00:45:42,576 --> 00:45:44,273
How's the competition prep going?

556
00:45:44,273 --> 00:45:50,283
Oh... It's been so long since I quit.
I'm just getting my feel back.

557
00:45:50,936 --> 00:45:53,816
You look like you could win
even if you competed today.

558
00:45:54,464 --> 00:45:56,416
I saw it myself.

559
00:45:57,783 --> 00:46:00,484
But that was real combat.

560
00:46:00,484 --> 00:46:03,149
Competition is different.

561
00:46:05,272 --> 00:46:08,249
You said you wanted to find out
what kind of person you are, right?

562
00:46:18,016 --> 00:46:20,087
From what I've seen,

563
00:46:20,087 --> 00:46:23,268
you're bright, honest, and brave.

564
00:46:23,268 --> 00:46:25,720
Decent and upright...

565
00:46:25,720 --> 00:46:29,438
Well, that's more or less right.

566
00:46:29,438 --> 00:46:34,236
You probably already
have a sense of what I'm like.

567
00:46:34,236 --> 00:46:36,428
So I think...

568
00:46:36,428 --> 00:46:40,068
you're probably thinking the same thing I am.

569
00:46:40,068 --> 00:46:42,164
The same...

570
00:46:42,164 --> 00:46:44,283
What are you thinking about?

571
00:46:45,452 --> 00:46:50,152
I guess we can't look toward the same future.

572
00:46:50,152 --> 00:46:51,852
That's what I was thinking.

573
00:46:54,380 --> 00:46:56,600
I was really glad to have met you.

574
00:46:56,600 --> 00:46:58,892
During our time together,

575
00:46:58,892 --> 00:47:00,652
I had so much fun.

576
00:47:03,604 --> 00:47:07,749
You'll become a great police officer.

577
00:47:07,749 --> 00:47:11,683
I'll always be cheering you on from afar.

578
00:47:26,716 --> 00:47:29,376
I'll make sure I become
a good police officer.

579
00:47:29,376 --> 00:47:31,583
Thank you, Assistant Manager Ki.

580
00:47:36,500 --> 00:47:40,028
If I leave again someday,
will you follow me then too?

581
00:47:40,028 --> 00:47:41,728
Are you going somewhere?

582
00:47:44,881 --> 00:47:46,268
Where would I even go?

583
00:47:46,268 --> 00:47:47,800
<i>Everything I need is right here.</i>

584
00:47:47,800 --> 00:47:51,449
She went alone this time.

585
00:47:56,980 --> 00:47:58,932
Stop moping around, and get up.

586
00:47:58,932 --> 00:48:00,632
Come on!

587
00:48:06,420 --> 00:48:09,684
From now on, come out
and eat with me at mealtimes.

588
00:48:09,684 --> 00:48:12,483
- People need to eat to live.
- I do eat.

589
00:48:12,483 --> 00:48:15,804
I mean real meals. Not random
snacks you use to get by.

590
00:48:15,804 --> 00:48:17,972
A warm meal!

591
00:48:17,972 --> 00:48:20,480
I eat proper meals sometimes.

592
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:23,548
And after we eat,
take a walk in the park with me.

593
00:48:23,548 --> 00:48:24,981
- What?
- Don't just hole up

594
00:48:24,981 --> 00:48:26,596
in that smelly little room.

595
00:48:26,596 --> 00:48:29,516
Get some fresh air once in a while, okay?

596
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:31,984
I do, sometimes.

597
00:48:31,984 --> 00:48:35,316
After our walk, let's go clothes shopping.

598
00:48:37,584 --> 00:48:41,049
You look like you've got a decent frame.

599
00:48:43,808 --> 00:48:46,820
Oh, I dress pretty well.

600
00:48:46,820 --> 00:48:48,988
This is all for my sake.

601
00:48:48,988 --> 00:48:52,452
Now that Director Yoo is gone,
who knows how often we'll go out together?

602
00:48:52,452 --> 00:48:54,649
So take good care of your condition.

603
00:48:59,812 --> 00:49:02,392
What are you doing? It'll get cold.

604
00:49:02,392 --> 00:49:04,092
Okay.

605
00:49:14,744 --> 00:49:17,128
Mommy.

606
00:49:17,128 --> 00:49:19,692
Mommy.

607
00:49:19,692 --> 00:49:21,884
Mommy.

608
00:49:21,884 --> 00:49:24,688
- Where are you, Mommy?
- Yul, what's wrong?

609
00:49:24,688 --> 00:49:27,783
When is Mommy coming?

610
00:49:30,132 --> 00:49:31,652
Yul,

611
00:49:31,652 --> 00:49:35,292
Mommy has so much work,
so she isn't finished yet.

612
00:49:35,292 --> 00:49:38,752
I miss Mommy,

613
00:49:38,752 --> 00:49:41,940
but I guess she doesn't miss me.

614
00:49:41,940 --> 00:49:44,208
Oh, no, that's not true.

615
00:49:44,208 --> 00:49:47,608
Mommy misses you so much,
so she cries every night.

616
00:49:47,608 --> 00:49:48,664
Really?

617
00:49:48,664 --> 00:49:51,264
Of course. It's true.

618
00:49:51,264 --> 00:49:52,849
Yul,

619
00:49:52,849 --> 00:49:57,980
Mommy also misses you,
but she's being strong and working hard.

620
00:49:57,980 --> 00:50:00,183
So what should Yul do?

621
00:50:01,772 --> 00:50:04,444
Yul should be brave and behave, right?

622
00:50:04,444 --> 00:50:06,849
That way, when Mommy comes home...

623
00:50:08,265 --> 00:50:12,492
When she comes home, wow,
she'll be so happy and say,

624
00:50:12,492 --> 00:50:15,716
"Wow, my Yul waited
so bravely for me," right?

625
00:50:16,740 --> 00:50:21,256
Until then, Yul will play,
eat, and sleep well.

626
00:50:21,256 --> 00:50:23,376
And Daddy will work hard.

627
00:50:23,376 --> 00:50:28,204
And we'll wait bravely for Mommy together.

628
00:50:28,204 --> 00:50:29,904
How's that?

629
00:50:34,820 --> 00:50:36,849
That's my good girl, Yul.

630
00:50:43,616 --> 00:50:45,183
[Siem Reap Mom-Daughter
Murder Case Relationship Chart]

631
00:50:45,183 --> 00:50:46,416
[July 24, 2025, Oh Seong Nam
and Han Deok Man entered Siem Reap]

632
00:50:46,416 --> 00:50:47,783
[Oh Seong Nam, Han Deok Man,
What is their connection? Tourism?]

633
00:50:47,783 --> 00:50:49,549
[Checklist, Inquire with local guides,
Find their connection]

634
00:50:52,283 --> 00:50:53,883
[Oh Seong Nam and Han Deok Man,
Need to verify the relationship]

635
00:50:53,883 --> 00:50:57,083
[Dark Web Bypass]

636
00:51:00,052 --> 00:51:01,052
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic]
Huh?

637
00:51:01,052 --> 00:51:02,408
[Onsang Middle School]
Huh?

638
00:51:02,408 --> 00:51:05,752
Mr. Kwon! Please take a look at this!

639
00:51:05,752 --> 00:51:08,580
You see Dr. Oh and Child Love here?

640
00:51:08,580 --> 00:51:11,064
It's an illegal site. Right here.

641
00:51:11,064 --> 00:51:12,416
This is evidence related to the case.

642
00:51:12,416 --> 00:51:16,100
It was faxed over to us
by the Cambodian police.

643
00:51:16,100 --> 00:51:18,872
Please check it just once.

644
00:51:18,872 --> 00:51:20,644
The chicken porridge is here.

645
00:51:20,644 --> 00:51:22,749
Wow, that looks good.

646
00:51:28,180 --> 00:51:31,307
- Mommy likes chicken porridge too.
- Right?

647
00:51:31,307 --> 00:51:32,836
- Mommy loves chicken porridge, right?
- Yeah.

648
00:51:32,836 --> 00:51:35,389
- Yeah.
- Is Daddy a good cook?

649
00:51:35,389 --> 00:51:36,412
You're pretty good.

650
00:51:36,412 --> 00:51:38,112
Thank you.

651
00:51:44,180 --> 00:51:46,312
Daddy, I'm all done cleaning up!

652
00:51:46,312 --> 00:51:47,532
Did you clean this all up yourself, Yul?

653
00:51:47,532 --> 00:51:49,649
- Yeah.
- Great job.

654
00:52:02,216 --> 00:52:03,860
[Exclusive: Kingfisher's Final Two Victims
Were Not Innocent Civilians]

655
00:52:03,860 --> 00:52:06,376
<i>Kingfisher's last two victims</i>

656
00:52:06,376 --> 00:52:08,549
<i>were not innocent civilians.</i>

657
00:52:09,392 --> 00:52:12,544
<i>The shocking truth about the two men</i>

658
00:52:12,544 --> 00:52:15,516
<i>believed to be Kingfisher's
final victims has finally come to light.</i>

659
00:52:15,516 --> 00:52:17,081
[Kingfisher's Final Two Victims]
<i>The two men, previously</i>

660
00:52:17,081 --> 00:52:18,868
[Exposed as Criminals]
<i>believed to have no connection,</i>

661
00:52:18,868 --> 00:52:20,600
<i>were confirmed to have stayed</i>

662
00:52:20,600 --> 00:52:24,120
<i>in the same Southeast Asian country
during the same period in the past.</i>

663
00:52:24,120 --> 00:52:28,271
<i>An investigation based on a tip
from a Korean media outlet</i>

664
00:52:28,271 --> 00:52:31,568
<i>and cooperation from local authorities
uncovered their plot</i>

665
00:52:31,568 --> 00:52:33,824
<i>and the murder of a mom and daughter.</i>

666
00:52:33,824 --> 00:52:37,012
<i>According to a joint investigation
by the media and police,</i>

667
00:52:37,012 --> 00:52:40,228
<i>the two men lured an eight-year-old girl</i>

668
00:52:40,228 --> 00:52:44,856
<i>selling food on the street
in a Southeast Asian country.</i>

669
00:52:44,856 --> 00:52:47,052
<i>When the girl's mom resisted
their attempt to sexually assault her,</i>

670
00:52:47,052 --> 00:52:49,396
<i>they brutally murdered both mom and daughter</i>

671
00:52:49,396 --> 00:52:52,000
<i>and disposed of their bodies.</i>

672
00:52:52,000 --> 00:52:55,492
<i>The two men, a practicing doctor
and a middle school teacher,</i>

673
00:52:55,492 --> 00:52:57,672
<i>were members of an illegal website</i>

674
00:52:57,672 --> 00:53:00,372
<i>sharing child sexual exploitation material.</i>

675
00:53:00,372 --> 00:53:02,912
<i>They met offline to plot the crime,</i>

676
00:53:02,912 --> 00:53:06,844
<i>and then pretended
to travel abroad separately</i>

677
00:53:06,844 --> 00:53:10,768
<i>before meeting there to carry it out.</i>

678
00:53:10,768 --> 00:53:12,622
Alright, everyone.

679
00:53:12,622 --> 00:53:13,724
Let's head out.

680
00:53:13,724 --> 00:53:15,492
Let's go!

681
00:53:15,492 --> 00:53:16,731
Let's go!

682
00:53:16,731 --> 00:53:18,431
Okay.

683
00:53:23,580 --> 00:53:24,844
What about Tae Min?

684
00:53:24,844 --> 00:53:25,848
Oh.

685
00:53:25,848 --> 00:53:27,716
Have a safe trip.

686
00:53:36,232 --> 00:53:41,064
<i>As the shocking crimes of the two men</i>

687
00:53:41,064 --> 00:53:43,283
<i>once believed to be innocent victims
of Kingfisher come to light,</i>

688
00:53:43,283 --> 00:53:46,516
<i>public opinion on Kingfisher
is changing again.</i>

689
00:53:46,516 --> 00:53:50,128
<i>"Kingfisher never hurt
innocent people after all."</i>

690
00:53:50,128 --> 00:53:52,383
<i>"I always believed in him..."</i>

691
00:53:54,860 --> 00:53:56,560
Look at him.

692
00:53:57,700 --> 00:54:01,183
He finally cleared Kingfisher's name.

693
00:54:31,032 --> 00:54:34,316
I need to clean up that place too.

694
00:54:43,244 --> 00:54:45,449
I wonder how Yoo Bo Na's story

695
00:54:46,752 --> 00:54:48,549
will end.

696
00:54:56,628 --> 00:54:59,200
Yul, Daddy is working late today,

697
00:54:59,200 --> 00:55:01,388
[6 Months Later]
so Auntie Se Ah will pick you up.

698
00:55:01,388 --> 00:55:02,451
Okay?

699
00:55:02,451 --> 00:55:04,976
Wash your hands as soon as you get home.

700
00:55:04,976 --> 00:55:09,668
Daddy made your favorite curry.
Eat up with Auntie Se Ah.

701
00:55:09,668 --> 00:55:11,960
My little precious,
you can do that for me, right?

702
00:55:11,960 --> 00:55:14,467
Yeah, I can.

703
00:55:14,467 --> 00:55:15,504
That's my Yul. You're the best.

704
00:55:15,504 --> 00:55:17,244
The best! The best!

705
00:55:17,244 --> 00:55:19,512
Mommy used to do it like this.

706
00:55:19,512 --> 00:55:21,426
The best! The best!

707
00:55:21,426 --> 00:55:23,349
Mommy did that?

708
00:55:24,952 --> 00:55:28,416
Huh? It's snowing. Daddy, look, it's snowing!

709
00:55:28,416 --> 00:55:30,549
Wow, snow!

710
00:55:38,860 --> 00:55:40,849
Want to go outside and see?

711
00:55:44,544 --> 00:55:48,624
Wow, there's so much white snow.

712
00:55:48,624 --> 00:55:51,821
It sure is. The first snow
came early this year.

713
00:55:51,821 --> 00:55:53,916
Wow, it's beautiful.

714
00:56:00,176 --> 00:56:03,172
My name is Yoo Bo Na. It's my real name.

715
00:56:03,172 --> 00:56:06,549
Please take good care of me.
It's my first time with love.

716
00:56:12,548 --> 00:56:14,248
It's beautiful.

717
00:57:03,844 --> 00:57:06,504
Any idea where she might have gone?

718
00:57:06,504 --> 00:57:08,596
I'm not sure.

719
00:57:08,596 --> 00:57:11,016
She's always been good at hiding.

720
00:57:11,816 --> 00:57:13,849
She's probably somewhere

721
00:57:14,549 --> 00:57:17,020
finding a view of her own.

722
00:57:17,020 --> 00:57:19,089
But three or four months later,

723
00:57:19,089 --> 00:57:20,704
she came back and asked us
to tear up her resignation.

724
00:57:20,704 --> 00:57:23,084
I asked her why.

725
00:57:23,084 --> 00:57:25,613
And she only said one thing.

726
00:57:25,613 --> 00:57:28,720
"I've seen a beautiful view."

727
00:57:28,720 --> 00:57:33,083
I wondered what beautiful view
she'd seen, and where,

728
00:57:33,083 --> 00:57:37,549
that brought someone who was
practically dead back to life like that.

729
00:57:39,672 --> 00:57:42,183
Seeing you, Mr. Kwon Tae Seong,
made me realize it.

730
00:57:42,183 --> 00:57:44,008
It was you.

731
00:57:44,008 --> 00:57:46,849
<i>You are the one who saved Director Yoo.</i>

732
00:58:36,948 --> 00:58:39,084
She never used to step outside.

733
00:58:39,084 --> 00:58:41,648
So I don't know what got into her
to go to the mountains.

734
00:58:41,648 --> 00:58:43,864
On a day like this too.

735
00:58:43,864 --> 00:58:45,983
The trail must be rough.

736
00:59:08,368 --> 00:59:10,708
<i>Merry Christmas!</i>

737
00:59:10,708 --> 00:59:15,049
This is a Christmas present for you, Bo Na!

738
00:59:16,102 --> 00:59:18,716
Aren't they beautiful and crystal clear?

739
00:59:19,696 --> 00:59:22,473
When I was little, I used to suck on them.

740
00:59:22,473 --> 00:59:25,116
We could make shaved ice with them, right?

741
00:59:30,808 --> 00:59:33,040
I was so scared.

742
00:59:33,040 --> 00:59:35,822
I was afraid you might disappear.

743
00:59:35,822 --> 00:59:38,305
Perhaps love begins

744
00:59:38,305 --> 00:59:40,068
when you find yourself drawn to

745
00:59:40,068 --> 00:59:43,312
just one side of a person
among all the many sides they have.

746
00:59:43,312 --> 00:59:45,549
<i>I've already fallen in love.</i>

747
01:00:14,796 --> 01:00:16,496
It's beautiful.

748
01:00:18,840 --> 01:00:21,896
This place is really
more beautiful in winter.

749
01:00:21,896 --> 01:00:23,596
Don't you think?

750
01:00:27,983 --> 01:00:30,496
This wildflower field
used to be the view of my life.

751
01:00:30,496 --> 01:00:33,628
But since then,
it has changed into a snowfield.

752
01:00:33,628 --> 01:00:38,300
I guess even your taste in scenery changes
depending on who you're with.

753
01:00:38,300 --> 01:00:40,849
If the flowers heard that,
would they feel a little hurt?

754
01:00:46,668 --> 01:00:49,998
The trail was rough,
so it took me forever to get up here.

755
01:00:49,998 --> 01:00:55,336
I was worried they'd close
the road because of the snow.

756
01:00:55,336 --> 01:00:57,883
But luckily, the mountain let me through.

757
01:00:58,532 --> 01:01:00,449
I slipped twice, though.

758
01:01:00,449 --> 01:01:04,516
I was in such a rush,
so I didn't bring the right shoes.

759
01:01:09,476 --> 01:01:11,176
I thought...

760
01:01:14,232 --> 01:01:16,982
I didn't need to know.

761
01:01:16,982 --> 01:01:19,449
Where you were born, how you grew up,

762
01:01:19,449 --> 01:01:22,608
what you do, how you live...

763
01:01:22,608 --> 01:01:24,648
I thought it was okay
not knowing any of that.

764
01:01:24,648 --> 01:01:27,383
Because the Yoo Bo Na I know
was enough for me.

765
01:01:28,124 --> 01:01:30,916
You eat chicken
and chicken porridge well now.

766
01:01:31,583 --> 01:01:35,764
And you tell Yul every day
to get along with her friends.

767
01:01:35,764 --> 01:01:37,464
You've got a mom

768
01:01:38,352 --> 01:01:41,928
and three sisters-in-law.

769
01:01:41,928 --> 01:01:44,016
You're not alone anymore.

770
01:01:45,769 --> 01:01:47,916
I know you so well now.

771
01:01:49,184 --> 01:01:53,083
And I love you more than
anyone in this world.

772
01:01:56,428 --> 01:01:58,483
But now I want to know.

773
01:02:01,249 --> 01:02:04,916
What was in your heart
as you walked that long road.

774
01:02:04,916 --> 01:02:07,508
How difficult it was.

775
01:02:07,508 --> 01:02:10,581
Whether you were lonely or scared. All of it.

776
01:02:10,581 --> 01:02:13,483
Every side of you that I don't know.

777
01:02:21,283 --> 01:02:23,983
I know we can't go back to how things were.

778
01:02:25,108 --> 01:02:26,732
But let's do this instead.

779
01:02:26,732 --> 01:02:28,816
Let's take our time
getting to know each other.

780
01:02:29,438 --> 01:02:31,138
Okay?

781
01:02:36,932 --> 01:02:39,916
So I can learn to love every side of you.

782
01:02:59,649 --> 01:03:02,340
Come home with me.

783
01:03:02,340 --> 01:03:04,416
It's freezing here.

784
01:03:09,144 --> 01:03:11,149
Yul's waiting for you too.

785
01:03:16,749 --> 01:03:20,516
I told her a wish
on the first snowfall comes true,

786
01:03:21,848 --> 01:03:24,683
and she wished to see her mommy.

787
01:03:25,604 --> 01:03:27,449
Just like me.

788
01:04:11,944 --> 01:04:14,149
There's something I've always wondered.

789
01:04:15,590 --> 01:04:17,290
What is it?

790
01:04:22,156 --> 01:04:23,728
Back during the World Cup...

791
01:04:23,728 --> 01:04:24,728
Yeah.

792
01:04:24,728 --> 01:04:26,992
Why did you report it for me?

793
01:04:26,992 --> 01:04:28,783
Because you were handsome

794
01:04:31,801 --> 01:04:33,816
and seemed like a good person.

795
01:04:37,883 --> 01:04:41,983
[Tae Seong Chicken]

796
01:04:44,983 --> 01:04:48,049
[Tae Seong Chicken]

797
01:05:02,964 --> 01:05:05,232
Good grief.

798
01:05:05,232 --> 01:05:08,464
Why are you always cleaning
whenever you get a chance?

799
01:05:08,464 --> 01:05:10,004
Are you still that thrilled?

800
01:05:10,004 --> 01:05:11,748
Of course, I am.

801
01:05:11,748 --> 01:05:14,281
It feels like I have everything in the world.

802
01:05:14,281 --> 01:05:17,436
Honestly, the more I think about it,
he's the landlord type.

803
01:05:17,436 --> 01:05:20,992
I mean, how could he sell
this place at that price?

804
01:05:20,992 --> 01:05:22,376
Exactly.

805
01:05:22,376 --> 01:05:25,720
We should be grateful he never
raised the rent all those years.

806
01:05:25,720 --> 01:05:28,112
Such a wonderful person.

807
01:05:28,112 --> 01:05:32,344
I thought we'd finally meet at the signing,
but he never showed up.

808
01:05:32,344 --> 01:05:34,044
I know.

809
01:05:34,804 --> 01:05:36,504
Oh, my.

810
01:05:37,120 --> 01:05:39,828
You used to say your whole life
was in this shop.

811
01:05:39,828 --> 01:05:42,512
And now your life is truly
in full bloom in your golden years, right?

812
01:05:42,512 --> 01:05:46,299
Absolutely. It's really my shop now.

813
01:05:46,299 --> 01:05:48,996
I'm putting my whole life into this!

814
01:05:48,996 --> 01:05:50,132
All in!

815
01:05:50,132 --> 01:05:52,416
Oh, is that so?

816
01:05:54,600 --> 01:05:56,599
Mom! We're going to be late.

817
01:05:56,599 --> 01:05:58,488
Oh, goodness, I almost forgot...

818
01:05:58,488 --> 01:06:00,777
Hold on, we should get going.

819
01:06:00,777 --> 01:06:03,800
You packed plenty of
snacks and drinks, right?

820
01:06:03,800 --> 01:06:05,332
- Tons of them.
- Okay.

821
01:06:05,332 --> 01:06:07,032
Let's hurry.

822
01:06:08,916 --> 01:06:11,116
Let's go!

823
01:06:13,516 --> 01:06:15,116
[Closed This Morning Due to a Family Event]

824
01:06:15,116 --> 01:06:17,416
[Exciting Sports Day]

825
01:06:21,490 --> 01:06:23,489
[Kwon Yul]
Yul!

826
01:06:23,489 --> 01:06:26,976
- Oh, there's Yul!
- Go, Kwon Yul! Fighting!

827
01:06:26,976 --> 01:06:29,156
Wow!

828
01:06:29,156 --> 01:06:31,276
Go, Blue Team!

829
01:06:31,276 --> 01:06:32,976
[We Love You, Ji An]
Hye Ri!

830
01:06:33,949 --> 01:06:34,983
Faster, faster!

831
01:06:34,983 --> 01:06:36,016
That's it!

832
01:06:36,016 --> 01:06:38,156
Come on, come on!

833
01:06:38,156 --> 01:06:40,349
Wow!

834
01:06:40,349 --> 01:06:42,183
[My Family's Little Precious]

835
01:06:42,816 --> 01:06:44,383
First place!

836
01:06:44,383 --> 01:06:45,883
Mommy, I got first place!

837
01:06:45,883 --> 01:06:47,949
- That's my girl! You're the best!
- First place!

838
01:06:47,949 --> 01:06:49,076
My little precious is the best!

839
01:06:49,076 --> 01:06:51,947
See? My national athlete blood runs deep.

840
01:06:51,947 --> 01:06:53,852
Why would your blood go to her?

841
01:06:53,852 --> 01:06:56,708
Oh, my. I guess she's so happy
with Mommy and Daddy here.

842
01:06:56,708 --> 01:06:58,949
My Yul is flying around all giddy today too!

843
01:06:58,949 --> 01:07:00,887
Kwon Yul is the best!

844
01:07:00,887 --> 01:07:04,883
Next up is the parents' relay race.

845
01:07:07,671 --> 01:07:10,568
See the calf muscles on number one
from the other team?

846
01:07:10,568 --> 01:07:12,480
- Yeah.
- She does

847
01:07:12,480 --> 01:07:13,749
PT at least three times a week.

848
01:07:13,749 --> 01:07:14,812
- Three times...
- Three...

849
01:07:14,812 --> 01:07:16,556
She's got a fast start.

850
01:07:16,556 --> 01:07:17,792
And runner number two.

851
01:07:17,792 --> 01:07:19,556
She keeps taking the weight onto
her left leg, right?

852
01:07:19,556 --> 01:07:21,764
- Her knee's bothering her.
- Okay.

853
01:07:21,764 --> 01:07:22,960
Oh!

854
01:07:22,960 --> 01:07:25,380
She'll lose speed on the turns.

855
01:07:25,380 --> 01:07:28,192
Runner number three is especially dangerous.

856
01:07:28,192 --> 01:07:30,805
- Why?
- Why?

857
01:07:30,805 --> 01:07:32,809
[Sol's Mom! Fighting!]
Sol's mom! Fighting!

858
01:07:32,809 --> 01:07:34,420
- Mommy!
- Good job!

859
01:07:34,420 --> 01:07:37,008
People like that are insanely competitive.

860
01:07:37,008 --> 01:07:39,752
Her eyes will go wild
the second she gets the baton.

861
01:07:39,752 --> 01:07:42,356
And runner number five over there.

862
01:07:42,356 --> 01:07:44,983
She arrived in heels
and just changed into sneakers.

863
01:07:44,983 --> 01:07:46,804
Oh, no.

864
01:07:46,804 --> 01:07:50,732
That literally screams,

865
01:07:50,732 --> 01:07:52,792
"You're all dead meat today."

866
01:07:52,792 --> 01:07:55,404
Okay, then I'll take the last leg.

867
01:07:55,404 --> 01:07:57,300
I'm an expert at killing it.

868
01:07:57,300 --> 01:07:59,004
Okay!

869
01:07:59,004 --> 01:08:00,080
Alright, okay!

870
01:08:00,080 --> 01:08:01,116
Shall we do this?

871
01:08:01,116 --> 01:08:02,472
- Let's crush them!
- Let's crush them!

872
01:08:02,472 --> 01:08:04,172
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

873
01:08:05,916 --> 01:08:08,749
- Let's go!
- It's okay even if you lose.

874
01:08:13,983 --> 01:08:17,149
[Red Team, Blue Team]

875
01:08:19,600 --> 01:08:21,300
Ready...

876
01:08:27,116 --> 01:08:28,916
[Run, You Got This!]

877
01:08:31,472 --> 01:08:33,172
Take it!

878
01:08:36,280 --> 01:08:38,949
- Hye Ri's mom!
- Hye Ri's mom, please!

879
01:08:43,183 --> 01:08:44,883
[Sol's Mom! Fighting!]

880
01:08:46,992 --> 01:08:49,449
- Go, Seo Jun's mom!
- Go, Seo Jun's mom!

881
01:08:51,788 --> 01:08:53,583
Isn't she a little slow?

882
01:08:53,583 --> 01:08:54,583
What's she doing?

883
01:08:54,583 --> 01:08:56,280
- Wait...
- Gosh.

884
01:08:56,280 --> 01:08:57,849
She was just all talk.

885
01:08:57,849 --> 01:08:59,604
- Alright, good!
- Let's go!

886
01:08:59,604 --> 01:09:00,616
That's it.

887
01:09:00,616 --> 01:09:01,916
Good, let's go!

888
01:09:01,916 --> 01:09:03,648
- Let's go! Run!
- You got this!

889
01:09:03,648 --> 01:09:05,348
Let's go!

890
01:09:18,416 --> 01:09:20,283
[Exciting Sports Day]

891
01:09:20,283 --> 01:09:21,983
[A Celebration of Young Dreams]

892
01:09:24,149 --> 01:09:25,883
[Rooting for You]

893
01:09:40,164 --> 01:09:41,508
Wow! At an incredible speed...

894
01:09:41,508 --> 01:09:43,360
- What happened to her?
- The final runner is charging ahead.

895
01:09:43,360 --> 01:09:45,348
She's closing the gap.

896
01:09:45,348 --> 01:09:47,440
- Go, Yoo Bo Na!
- And now, the final runner...

897
01:09:47,440 --> 01:09:50,283
- One more lap!
- Go, Mommy!

898
01:10:07,583 --> 01:10:09,183
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

899
01:10:09,183 --> 01:10:10,983
Wow!

900
01:10:22,160 --> 01:10:23,883
What did I just see?

901
01:10:23,883 --> 01:10:25,983
Yul got it from her mommy.

902
01:10:25,983 --> 01:10:28,816
What did she do back in the day?

903
01:10:28,816 --> 01:10:31,083
That's some serious
wasted talent in every way.

904
01:10:31,083 --> 01:10:35,483
I'm so proud of my daughter-in-law!

905
01:10:48,408 --> 01:10:50,108
Good grief.

906
01:10:53,328 --> 01:10:55,583
- Jeez.
- Wow!

907
01:10:56,448 --> 01:10:57,572
Gosh, you scared me!

908
01:10:57,572 --> 01:11:00,424
Slacking off instead of working, huh?

909
01:11:00,424 --> 01:11:02,749
Oh, come on.

910
01:11:04,340 --> 01:11:06,549
I'm not slacking.

911
01:11:07,483 --> 01:11:09,904
I'm just taking a break from the sun.

912
01:11:09,904 --> 01:11:11,276
I thought I'd get roasted alive.

913
01:11:11,276 --> 01:11:13,720
So why do you keep making
life hard for yourself?

914
01:11:13,720 --> 01:11:16,583
Out of everyone on earth, you'd be
the first cop to turn down a promotion,

915
01:11:16,583 --> 01:11:19,664
a reward, and then volunteer to be demoted.

916
01:11:19,664 --> 01:11:20,972
Look who's talking!

917
01:11:20,972 --> 01:11:22,375
Then is it common for a reporter to refuse

918
01:11:22,375 --> 01:11:24,616
the "Journalist of the Year Award," huh?

919
01:11:26,988 --> 01:11:28,688
Jeez.

920
01:11:30,376 --> 01:11:32,744
There are still plenty of bad guys out there.

921
01:11:32,744 --> 01:11:35,920
That's why I'm taking all the heat.

922
01:11:35,920 --> 01:11:38,048
People are demanding Kingfisher back.

923
01:11:38,048 --> 01:11:42,296
People always miss things that don't exist.

924
01:11:42,296 --> 01:11:45,440
Jeez, they should look for that
in fantasy stories.

925
01:11:45,440 --> 01:11:48,616
So go back to your place
and do your job, okay?

926
01:11:48,616 --> 01:11:52,140
Make sure another one doesn't pop up!

927
01:11:52,140 --> 01:11:53,784
Of course, I will.

928
01:11:53,784 --> 01:11:55,484
Jeez.

929
01:11:58,308 --> 01:12:01,200
You do your job properly too, Kwon Tae Seong!

930
01:12:01,200 --> 01:12:02,616
I always do.

931
01:12:02,616 --> 01:12:04,900
Unbelievable...

932
01:12:04,900 --> 01:12:06,649
Jeez.

933
01:12:35,983 --> 01:12:38,083
[Three Bears]

934
01:13:06,620 --> 01:13:08,348
<i>A woman in her 30s was found</i>

935
01:13:08,348 --> 01:13:12,024
<i>stabbed to death in a residential
neighborhood in Seoul this morning.</i>

936
01:13:12,024 --> 01:13:13,931
<i>Police say the man, in his 40s,</i>

937
01:13:13,931 --> 01:13:16,540
<i>had served time
for stalking the woman for years.</i>

938
01:13:16,540 --> 01:13:18,750
<i>They believe he killed her in retaliation</i>

939
01:13:18,750 --> 01:13:21,200
<i>after she reported him,
following his release,</i>

940
01:13:21,200 --> 01:13:24,424
<i>and are currently searching
for the suspect, who fled the scene.</i>

941
01:13:24,424 --> 01:13:26,408
<i>The victim reportedly
told people close to her</i>

942
01:13:26,408 --> 01:13:28,844
<i>that she feared he would come
after her once he was released.</i>

943
01:13:28,844 --> 01:13:30,746
[Victim Reportedly Feared Retaliation]
<i>She was said to have been</i>

944
01:13:30,746 --> 01:13:32,656
[After His Release]
<i>extremely distressed.</i>

945
01:13:32,656 --> 01:13:35,704
<i>As public concern grows over
recurring retaliatory crimes,</i>

946
01:13:35,704 --> 01:13:39,749
<i>police are focusing their efforts
on apprehending the suspect.</i>

947
01:13:40,604 --> 01:13:42,304
Yeah.

948
01:13:45,104 --> 01:13:47,849
Okay. Shall we go?

949
01:15:44,383 --> 01:15:46,133
[Thank you to all our viewers!]

950
01:15:46,133 --> 01:15:48,483
[May you all find your own beautiful view!]
